## Introduction
Most developers should know the benefits of writing docs in `.md`. Markdown not only gives you full ownership of all of your files, but also enables integration of arbitrary tools. Especially in the AI age, this is an essential strength. 
Integrating AI into your notes becomes as easy as just spawning an agent in your vault root and formulating some behaviour rules.
You aren't dependent on any toolset given to you by a firm with the same audience as scam callers.

*Choosing Obsidian means configurability, stability and (generally) a feeling of superiority.*

But like every highly configurable tool, it needs some setup to be nice to use. I've seen many bad tutorials and tips, and want to work my own experience into a small guide.
I built my vault to meet specifically my needs as a MINT student.

## The vault
I've used the software for 4 years now. I've installed (and uninstalled) hundreds of community plugins and was in configuration hell, a minimalism trip and everything in between. I think I found a nice middle ground that works for me.

Believe it or not, but I found the builtin link system (and thus the infamous obsidian [graph network](https://forum.obsidian.md/uploads/default/original/3X/6/0/604d3693c38722b0c4b29628df1d45ffa473dd0a.png)) as completely useless. That goes against the whole "second brain" crowd and I'm proud of it.
When I study, am completely organized into semesters, courses and lectures. Seeing the hierarchy?
Specific lecture notes correspond to specific lecture slides and embedded assets correspond to specific files.

*Connections in my vault aren't made via links, they are made with locations and the hierarchy that this creates, so why would I need any more links?*

```
.
├── Archive/
│   ├── SS25/
│   │   └── Course1
│   └── ...
├── Course2/
│   ├── assets/
│   │   └── Lecture01/
│   │       └── image.png
│   ├── Assignments/
│   ├── Exam-prep/
│   ├── ...
│   ├── LecturePDF/
│   │   ├── Lecture01.pdf
│   │   └── Lecture02.pdf
│   ├── Lecture01.md
│   └── Lecture02.md
└── Course3/
    └── ...
```

